The new early-exit block in `tumbleWindow` calls `doPayload(listener)` but is missing a `return` statement. After the listener is invoked, execution falls through to the subsequent `if (currentStage > matcher.firstPositiveStage && ...)` block and the rest of the method body. This can cause the listener to be invoked a second time (e.g., if `restartWindowFromTailQuery` is false, `doPayload` is called again; or the method continues to its normal completion path which also calls `doPayload`). A double-invocation of an `ActionListener` is undefined behavior and will likely cause a `RuntimeException` or silent data corruption.
Fix:
```java
if (allowPartialSequenceResults == false && shardFailures.isEmpty() == false) {
    doPayload(listener);
    return;
}
```

